1. Scope

"Software" means the KSL interpreter, its source code, documentation, and
modified versions of those materials. A program independently written in the
KSL language is not the Software merely because it was written in KSL.

2. Permission to use and share

Subject to section 3, you may use, study, copy, and modify the Software for
any purpose. You may distribute the Software or modified versions without
charge, provided you include this license and the copyright notice with every
copy and do not misrepresent a modified version as an official KSL release.

You may create, use, distribute, and sell programs independently written in
KSL without paying a fee or requesting permission under this license. Those
programs belong to their respective authors. This paragraph does not grant
permission to bundle or distribute the KSL interpreter or runtime itself as
part of a paid product.

3. Commercial exploitation of KSL

You must obtain a separate written agreement signed by the copyright holder
before you sell, license for a fee, or otherwise distribute the Software for
commercial advantage or monetary compensation. The same requirement applies
to including the Software in a paid product or charging for hosted access to
the Software itself. It applies to modified versions as well.

The separate agreement must specify a positive share of profit for the
copyright holder, the definition and calculation of that profit, reporting
periods, and payment terms. Requesting permission does not grant it. Until
the agreement is signed, no permission for these commercial activities is
granted.

4. Other rights and termination

This license does not grant rights to the KSL name, logos, or other trademarks.
If you violate this license, your permissions under it terminate. The
copyright holder may reinstate them in writing. Rights in independently
written KSL programs are unaffected.

5. Disclaimer

The Software is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, to the
extent permitted by applicable law. The copyright holder is not liable for
claims or damages arising from use of the Software, to the extent permitted
by applicable law.
